# The Pixel 7 Pro's declaration that suspend with the modem up is verified:
# MODEM-PLAN M6 passed on the reference phone on 2026-11-14 (sleeps, sleeps
# refused early with data busy, a text and a call each waking the phone),
# and its long check (SUSPEND-PLAN M6-D) on 2026-11-15
# (device/cheetah/SUSPEND-PLAN.md). With this file omamobile-modem's sleep
# policy skips the modem's sleep inhibitor at boot, but only on a kernel
# whose modem link refuses a sleep early while the link is up
# (linux-omarchy-mobile#232, kernel-2026.11.15 and later), and not where the
# owner has opted out (/etc/omamobile/modem-suspend-disable). It came out
# in 0.1.59 when mobile data died across sleeps (the network dropped the
# internet bearer and nothing set it up again) and is back in 0.1.60 with
# omamobile-modem-sit 0.3.42's reconnect, which M6-D passed on 2026-11-15
# (85 wakes in 45 minutes, nine bearer drops each set up again).
# No other device package ships it.
